course: dictionary
lesson: 4836
title: Names in the sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Hyades is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. It is a proper noun, which means it names one special thing. Here the thing is a group of stars.
explain: «Taurus has the V-shaped Hyades and the Pleiades, and Gemini has the twin stars Castor and Pollux, both high on winter evenings in the north.» The clue is V-shaped: the Hyades make a V shape in the sky. Taurus and Gemini are star patterns, so the Hyades must be stars too.
explain: Some names have more than one meaning. In old Greek myths, the Hyades were nymphs, daughters of Atlas, and they were linked with rain. When you meet a name, read the sentence around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: The Hyades are a cluster of stars in the constellation Taurus.
fact: A cluster is a group of things close together, so a star cluster is a group of stars close together.
fact: The Hyades are shaped like a V.
fact: The Hyades are the closest star cluster to Earth, about 150 light years away.
fact: A light year is the distance light travels in one year, so it measures distance, not time.
fact: In Greek myths, the Hyades were nymphs, daughters of Atlas, linked with rain.
exercise: «Taurus has the V-shaped Hyades and the Pleiades.» What shape are the Hyades? | Long and thin like a snake | *V-shaped | Square like a box | Round like a ball
exercise: The Hyades are a cluster of stars. What does cluster mean here? | A cloud of dust on Earth | *A group of things close together | A single very bright star | A storm of rain
exercise: In Greek myths, the Hyades were linked with which thing? | Snow | Wind | *Rain | Fire
test: In which constellation are the Hyades found? | Gemini | Orion | *Taurus | Ursa Major
test: The Hyades are near a bright red star. Which star is it? | Polaris | Vega | Sirius | *Aldebaran
exam: The Hyades are the closest star cluster to Earth. About how far away are they? | About 150 years | *About 150 light years | About 150 kilometres | About 150 metres
